Mythix DualShock 4 for xinput, proton_10.0 tree (MYTHIX_DS4_GLYPHS=1)
====================================================================

Origin : Luna's xinput DS4 work in Neutron-11.0-21199 (patches/mythix-ds4-xinput),
         carried to the proton_10.0 xinput. That xinput reads pads on an update
         thread with per-controller locks, so this is a port of the behaviour,
         not of the hunks.
Applies: the mythix-10.17 tree. Fix 39 resets dlls/xinput1_3/main.c to the
         proton_10.0 file before patch groups run, so this is its base.

What it does (dlls/xinput1_3/main.c, shared by xinput1_1..1_4 and xinputuap;
xinput9_1_0 forwards to xinput1_4 here):
  * MYTHIX_DS4_GLYPHS=1: Sony pads (VID 054c) report "not connected" to
    XInputGetState(Ex) and XInputGetKeystroke, so games with native PlayStation
    support use HID (PlayStation glyphs). XInputGetCapabilities still succeeds
    and XInputSetState still rumbles the pad.
  * Sony direct path: winebus keeps a hidraw DS4 / DualSense as plain HID, so
    when XInput slot 0 is empty the first Sony gamepad collection is opened
    there. Its reports are read on the update thread in the pad's own layout
    (USB report 0x01; winebus turns Bluetooth reports into it), and rumble
    goes through winebus' haptics reports (USB and Bluetooth), or a native
    0x05 report when the descriptor has none. A Steam Input virtual pad that
    claims the slot replaces it.
  * records each controller's vendor and product ID.
